cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "GENCO infers missing bus voltages zero-shot, and 3% of its pretraining labels are collapsed power-flow roots"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Al-Mahrouqi"
    given-names: "Mazin"
    affiliation: "The Ohio State University"
    email: "mahrouqi.1@osu.edu"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahrouqi1/grid-operations-genco"
abstract: "An audit of the released GridFM GENCO pretraining data and tests of the released checkpoint without fine-tuning: about 3% of the sampled pretraining labels are collapsed power-flow roots from the data generator; GENCO infers missing bus voltage magnitudes better than graph interpolation once 30% or more of bus voltages are measured (11 to 12 of 15 benchmark grids), but less accurately than a weighted-least-squares state estimator; continued pretraining did not improve it on a 15-grid benchmark; zero-shot power flow matches the limitation the GENCO paper states. Code, small result files, figure scripts and a one-command reproduction (bash reproduce.sh). Code is Apache-2.0; result files and figures are CC BY 4.0."
keywords:
  - power flow
  - graph foundation model
  - GENCO
  - GridFM
